<main class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Your information</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="notice"><strong>Status:</strong> This policy describes the current public site implementation reviewed on 12 November 2026 and should be checked again before new analytics, ads, accounts or other services are enabled.</p>
<h2>What information is processed</h2>
<p>EvonyMasters currently offers public tools without requiring you to create an account on this site. When you browse, the hosting and security providers may process technical request information such as IP address, browser and device information, timestamps and requested pages to serve the website and protect it from abuse.</p>
<p>Search terms, filters and tool inputs are sent to EvonyMasters' reward-search or calendar services when you use tools that need current data. This information is used to respond to the request. We do not ask for your Evony login credentials.</p>
<h2>Hosting and service providers</h2>
<p>The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, and its live reward and calendar requests use Cloudflare Workers. Cloudflare may handle technical request data as described in its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>. Source-code and feedback links may take you to GitHub, which has its own privacy practices.</p>
<h2>Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
<p>The site source reviewed for this policy does not include a Google AdSense, Google Analytics or other dedicated site-analytics script. This does not independently establish what hosting-level analytics or security features may be enabled in Cloudflare's account settings. Hosting and security services may use technical storage or cookies when needed to operate and secure the site.</p>
<p><strong>Advertising is planned, not represented as currently active.</strong> Before launching Google AdSense or new analytics, we intend to update this policy with the actual providers, purposes and applicable consent choices. Where required, visitors will be offered appropriate consent controls.</p>
<h2>Feedback and external sites</h2>
<p>The <a href="/contact/">feedback page</a> links to public GitHub issues. Any information you voluntarily post there may be visible publicly and governed by GitHub's terms. Avoid including personal or account-sensitive information. Links to third-party websites are subject to those sites' policies.</p>
<h2>Data requests and questions</h2>
<p>For feedback or questions about the site, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Do not post sensitive personal information in a public GitHub issue. If a private privacy-contact channel becomes available, it will be identified here.</p>
<h2>Updates</h2><p>We may revise this page when site features, service providers or privacy requirements change. The date shown at the top identifies the current published version.</p>
